CODEBASE EXPLORATION RULES:
1. ALWAYS extract key terms and concepts from user requests first
2. SYSTEMATICALLY search for these keywords in the codebase using grep_search
3. THOROUGHLY examine found code snippets before proposing solutions
4. PRIORITIZE exploration in this order:
   - Exact keyword matches in filenames and code
   - Related concepts and patterns
   - Parent and child components/dependencies
5. ALWAYS trace function call chains after identifying relevant code
   - Document the execution path and control flow
   - Map function inputs to outputs
   - Identify all return values and their usage
6. SYSTEMATICALLY analyze asynchronous operations
   - Trace promises, callbacks, and event listeners
   - Document event emissions and subscriptions
   - Map async/await patterns and their resolution paths
7. THOROUGHLY investigate database interactions
   - Identify all model definitions and relationships
   - Document CRUD operations on each model
   - Map database schema to application objects
8. COMPREHENSIVELY document side effects
   - Identify state mutations
   - Trace event propagation
   - Document external system interactions
   - Note performance implications
9. DOCUMENT all findings with precise file locations and line numbers
   - Include which search terms revealed each result
   - Note relationships between components

